  "evidence": "Manifest 0xc5ffa20 registers three descriptors. Each page allocates a separate state pointer and its destroy callback frees and clears that pointer. Detail page registers timer 0xc6003b8 at 1000 ms; when its state and labels exist, it calls the refresh helper 0xc5ffea0. Main and list functions set the named images, labels and event registrations.",
  "scope": "Page lifecycle pointer slots and listed setter/registration call sites. List callbacks can run repeatedly for different items; initial and timer-refresh labels use different call sites.",
